{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775350588-ZGpdi4D1fcPzdWCbbNle","role":"assistant","created":1775350639,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the NASA outlay data from both documents. Let me extract the total outlays (on-budget + off-budget) for NASA from FY 2008-2017.\n\nFrom 2012 bulletin (page 24):\n- 2008: 17,834\n- 2009: 19,168\n- 2010: 18,906\n- 2011: 17,617\n- 2012: 17,190\n\nFrom 2017 bulletin (page 22):\n- 2013: 16,978\n- 2014: 17,093\n- 2015: 18,272\n- 2016: 18,828\n- 2017: 18,698\n\nThese values are in millions of dollars. So I need to convert to billions (divide by 1000).\n\nNow I need to calculate the 10% Winsorized range. The 10% Winsorized range involves:\n1. Sorting the data\n2. Replacing the bottom 10% of values with the next higher value\n3. Replacing the top 10% of values with the next lower value\n4. Then calculating the range (max - min)\n\nLet me calculate:\n- Total of 10 years: FY 2008-2017 = 10 values\n- 10% of 10 = 1 value\n\nSo for 10% Winsorization:\n- Bottom 10%: replace 1 lowest value with the next lowest\n- Top 10%: replace 1 highest value with the next highest\n\nThe values in millions:\n17,834 (2008)\n19,168 (2009)\n18,906 (2010)\n17,617 (2011)\n17,190 (2012)\n16,978 (2013)\n17,093 (2014)\n18,272 (2015)\n18,828 (2016)\n18,698 (2017)\n\nLet me sort these:\n16,978 (2013)\n17,093 (2014)\n\n\n17,190 (2012)\n17,617 (2011)\n17,834 (2008)\n18,272 (2015)\n18,698 (2017)\n18,828 (2016)\n18,906 (2010)\n19,168 (2009)\n\nAfter sorting: 16,978, 17,093, 17,190, 17,617, 17,834, 18,272, 18,698, 18,828, 18,906, 19,168\n\nFor 10% Winsorization with 10 values (1 each side):\n- Bottom 10%: replace 16,978 with 17,093 (the next lowest)\n- Top 10%: replace 19,168 with 18,906 (the next highest)\n\nWinsorized set becomes: 17,093, 17,093, 17,190, 17,617, 17,834, 18,272, 18,698, 18,828, 18,906, 18,906\n\nThe range is 18,906 - 17,093 = 1,813 million, or 1.813 billion dollars.\n\nFor the 10% Winsorized range with 10 values, I need to identify the lowest and highest values. The bottom value is 16,978 and the top value is 19,168. Since these each represent 10% of the dataset, they get replaced with the next values: 17,093 at the bottom and 18,906 at the top. This gives a range of 18,906 - 17,093 = 1,813 million, or 1.81 billion dollars when rounded to the hundredths place.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_53c0ea022916dc83","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# NASA outlay data (in millions) from the bulletins\n# FY 2008-2012 from 2012 bulletin\n# FY 2013-2017 from 2017 bulletin\n\nnasa_outlays = {\n    2008: 17834,\n    2009: 19168,\n    2010: 18906,\n    2011: 17617,\n    2012: 17190,\n    2013: 16978,\n    2014: 17093,\n    2015: 18272,\n    2016: 18828,\n    2017: 18698\n}\n\n# Convert to billions\nvalues = [v/1000 for v in nasa_outlays.values()]\nprint(\"NASA total outlays (on+off budget) in billions:\")\nfor year, val in nasa_outlays.items():\n    print(f\"  {year}: {val/1000:.3f}\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nValues in billions: {sorted(values)}\")\n\n# Calculate 10% Winsorized range\n# n = 10, 10% of 10 = 1\n# Replace bottom 10% (1 value) with next lowest\n# Replace top 10% (1 value) with next highest\n\nsorted_vals = sorted(values)\nprint(f\"\\nSorted values: {sorted_vals}\")\n\n# For 10% Winsorization: \n# The 10th percentile = sorted[0] (replace with sorted[1])\n# The 90th percentile = sorted[-1] (replace with sorted[-2])\n\nwinsorized = sorted_vals.copy()\nwinsorized[0] = sorted_vals[1]  # Replace lowest with 2nd lowest\nwinsorized[-1] = sorted_vals[-2]  # Replace highest with 2nd highest\n\nprint(f\"\\nWinsorized values: {winsorized}\")\nprint(f\"Original min: {min(values):.4f}, max: {max(values):.4f}\")\nprint(f\"Winsorized min: {min(winsorized):.4f}, max: {max(winsorized):.4f}\")\n\nwinsorized_range = max(winsorized) - min(winsorized)\nprint(f\"\\n10% Winsorized range: {winsorized_range:.4f} billion dollars\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to hundredths: {winsorized_range:.2f}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
