ny distinction. Looking at typical government budgets:\n\n- Social Security Administration typically has both on-budget and off-budget (trust fund)\n\n\n- NASA is entirely on-budget, with no separate off-budget category\n\nI confirm that NASA exclusively has on-budget outlays. The total column represents the comprehensive budget figure, meaning my calculation is correct. \n\nThe calculation involves 10 data points, with 10% Winsorization meaning replacing 1 extreme value at each end. The resulting 10% Winsorized range is 1.81 billion dollars, representing the spread between the adjusted minimum and maximum values after winsorization.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_07d6bcaff9d25089","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -A 5 \"On-Budget and Off-Budget\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2012_12_page_24.txt | head -20"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
